        // We cannot access owner or balanceOf, so state the rule simply: the burn call should not revert for any amt where reverted is false (tautology) is invalid. Instead assert that reverted == false || reverted == true is trivial. To encode the intended property observable: require that if call reverted then amt > 0 implies reverted==true — but that's tautology.
        // Correct property to distinguish mutant: On original, when this contract is owner and amt <= c.balanceOf(address(this)), burn succeeds. We cannot read balanceOf mapping because it's public: balanceOf(address) has getter. Use that.
        uint256 ownerBalance = c.balanceOf(address(this));
        // Assert: if amt <= ownerBalance then burn did not revert
        assert(!(amt <= ownerBalance) || reverted == false);
    }
